  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When capacitor is fully charged, then it acts like a open switch, therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math> resistor has no use. So, rest of the resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math> will be in series. Hence, current drawn from cell</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>"
  }
